## 🔴 BUG FIX FIRST — CSV Export Auth Token (Critical)

### Root Cause
`window.open('/api/...')` opens a plain browser tab with **no `Authorization: Bearer` header** — the server returns `401 Unauthorized`, which users see as a vague "token" error.

### Fix Strategy
Replace all `window.open()` CSV calls with **fetch-then-blob-download** pattern using the axios instance (which already injects the JWT).

#### Files to Fix
- [`LiveSessionView.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/JAYLO/Downloads/ccdi-qrscan/ccdi-qrscan/client/src/pages/instructor/LiveSessionView.jsx) — `downloadSessionCSV()`
- [`SectionDetailsPage.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/JAYLO/Downloads/ccdi-qrscan/ccdi-qrscan/client/src/pages/instructor/SectionDetailsPage.jsx) — `downloadTermCSV()`
- [`AttendanceInsightsPage.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/JAYLO/Downloads/ccdi-qrscan/ccdi-qrscan/client/src/pages/instructor/AttendanceInsightsPage.jsx) — all report downloads

**Pattern:**
```js
const downloadCSV = async (url, filename) => {
  const res = await api.get(url, { responseType: 'blob' });
  const href = URL.createObjectURL(res.data);
  const a = document.createElement('a');
  a.href = href; a.download = filename; a.click();
  URL.revokeObjectURL(href);
};
```

